  "slug": "aware-topic-51b6",
  "summary": "Benchmarks now test whether AI agents can execute genomics and single-cell analyses, with best reported GeneBench-Pro pass rate at 31.5%.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread across these items is evaluation and automation of biological analysis by LLM-based agents. Prompt-to-Paper grounds manuscript claims in retrieved literature and executes bioinformatics experiments with quality scoring. GeneBench-Pro and BAISBench test agents on statistical reasoning and on real single-cell transcriptomic discovery, with GeneBench-Pro reporting a best pass rate of 31.5% across 129 problems. Agentomics autonomously develops biomedical ML solutions across 20 datasets, including protein engineering. What is new is that agent execution itself is now the object of measurement, with reported results indicating substantial remaining gaps. These items share an agentic focus but differ in whether they build systems or evaluate them.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-07-05"
}
